  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1153 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nA low amplitude jet stream is expected to set up across the CONUS on \nFriday with zonal flow stretching from the West Coast to the Plain. \nA surface low will develop in eastern Colorado and quickly push \nnortheast, which will cause the surface winds in the Panhandles to \nturn southerly to southwesterly at 10-20 mph. We'll see temperatures \nbecome hot again, ranging from the mid-90s to low-100s, and given \nthe overall lack of forcing, expecting it to be a dry day. \n\nWe'll see the jet stream become even more zonal across the CONUS on \nSaturday. A very weak 700mb shortwave is forecast to move into the \nPanhandles and create a low-end chance for thunderstorms across the \neastern Panhandles. \n\nGetting into Sunday, a Fall-like shortwave trough is forecast to \ntrack from the Intermountain West into the Upper Midwest. This \nsteepened surface pressure gradient will cause surface winds to \nstrengthen across the Panhandles into the 15 to potentially even 25 \nmph range. This may lead to elevated fire weather conditions, but it \nwill certainly depend upon how much rain falls leading up to Sunday. \nThunderstorms that develop in New Mexico may try to work into the \nwestern Panhandles Sunday evening, but confidence is very low at \nthis time.\n\nConfidence in the forecast substantially decreases Monday and \nbeyond. A cold front associated with the aforementioned Midwestern \ntrough is expected to barrel into the Plains, but there is a wide \nrange of outcomes with that front. This includes the potential for a \nsignificant cooldown with a low percentage of ensemble members \nsuggesting highs could be in the 70s to 80s on Tuesday and \nWednesday. Another factor that will need to be monitored is the \npotential for moving into an active weather pattern; the NBM already \nhas 30-50% PoPs from Monday through Wednesday. However, that seems \nquite ambitious for being 6-8 days out and lacking a large synoptic \nsystem , but overall, it is apparent that the pattern could turn \nmore active next week.\n\nVanden Bosch",
